From 695d193c9f64c10bf1396b8355486cc08deb45d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: XCH27 <49464716+XCH27@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 14:37:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Plugins contribute views: MCP Apps ui:// resources from their
 own server, shown in the side pane (OV-100 phase 4)

A plugin declares fleet.views[] naming one of its MCP servers and a ui://
resource. The workspace runtime reads that resource and proxies tools/call
only to that server, so a person in the view and an Agent in a conversation
call the same operations; a disabled plugin or one awaiting approval has no
runnable server and its view does not open. The renderer shows the view as
a Project-wide side-pane tab in an opaque-origin iframe under the MCP Apps
default CSP plus the domains the resource declared, answers ui/initialize
with Fleet theme tokens and follows theme changes. Views appear in the side
pane launcher and + menu. The MCP port gains readResource.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
